  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is about a mismatch when viewing your own profile page vs what other people see when they look at your profile page. \nWhen viewing your own bio/profile page, it shows private worlds under \"Uploaded Worlds\". The same applies to viewing a world page, under \"More From This Author.\" Other people only see your public worlds here. It would be nice if you also saw the same thing.\nI believe the old menu also only showed your own public worlds when looking at your own profile.\nSince I can already see my own private worlds in the My Worlds/Uploaded category I feel like having them on the bio page is not necessary and kind of confusing.\nAs a creator with a lot of worlds I would like the profile page this to be the place I go to to see all my public-only worlds in one place and their player counts, and to see what everyone else sees when they open my profile because the page is a common conversation topic when I meet new people and fans on VRC.\nPerhaps your self-profile-page tab is meant to be a shortcut for all your worlds, avatars, and playlists? Since you can see all your avatars (including private) and playlists (including private) here.\nIf so, it would be nice to at least have a checkbox to hide private worlds from this list, like there is when you look at your own profile page on the website.",
